  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Delighted with his molecular lunch, Nastya's father prepares to sign the contract with his business partners and asks Max to pop a bottle of champagne right at the table.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вам понравилось?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ты знаешь, вкусно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ну что, господа, подпишем?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Конечно! Надо это обмыть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Шампанского!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я сейчас открою и принесу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Что значит открою? Здесь открывай.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "И последняя подпись вот здесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Извините! Простите!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ваш ужин за наш счёт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "А где у вас здесь туалет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я вас провожу.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вам понравилось?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you like it?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'you' and finishing on 'pleased'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ты знаешь, вкусно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You know, it is delicious.' The grammar packs 'you' and 'deliciously' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Ну что, господа, подпишем?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well then, gentlemen, shall we sign?' Notice how Russian expresses 'come on' and 'will sign' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Конечно! Надо это обмыть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Of course! We need to celebrate this with a drink.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'of course' before landing on 'to celebrate with a drink'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Шампанского!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Some champagne!' the guest brings out the contrast between 'champagne' and 'champagne' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я сейчас открою и принесу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will open it right now and bring it.' Max anchors the line on 'I', while 'will bring' completes the thought. the guest answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Что значит открою? Здесь открывай.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What do you mean 'I will open it'? Open it here.' The grammar packs 'what' and 'open' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "И последняя подпись вот здесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And the last signature right here.' The meaning hinges on 'and' working together with 'here' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Извините! Простите!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Excuse me! Forgive me!' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'excuse me' and finishing on 'forgive'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ваш ужин за наш счёт.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Your dinner is on the house.' Max anchors the line on 'your', while 'score' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "А где у вас здесь туалет?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And where is the restroom here?' In Russian, the idea of 'and' flows naturally into 'restroom' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я вас провожу.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will show you the way.' Notice how Russian expresses 'I' and 'will escort' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
